  m_text: Nonograms, also known as Hanjie, Paint by Numbers, Picross, Griddlers,
    and Pic-a-Pix are picture logic puzzles in which cells in a grid must be colored
    or left blank according to numbers at the edges of the grid to reveal a hidden
    picture. In this puzzle, the numbers are a form of discrete tomography that measures
    how many unbroken lines of filled-in squares there are in any given row or column.
